  "implementationContract": [
    "Same ownedKey verifies exact one same-Keychain private signing key and public-key equality; only its borrowed CSSM reference BlobType/private class/sign header is checked. KeyData is never read/copied/exported; its public borrowed lifetime remains under SecKey.",
    "Existing classic ACL append is unchanged. New public CSSM_ChangeKeyAcl ADD only executes when no partition exists, using the exact typed PARTITION subject, PARTITION_ID authorization and protected partition tag.",
    "Only four entries: apple-tool:, apple:, codesign:, and the exact currently executing valid ad-hoc-signed importer cdhash. Current dynamic/static signatures and 20-byte unique identifier are checked via public APIs; unsigned, non-ad-hoc/team and abnormal identifiers are refused. It does not re-sign the importer or any target.",
    "Actual database password is a bounded private CSSM KEYCHAIN_LOCK/PASSWORD/DATUM credential without UI callback. The 256-byte local copy is volatile-cleared on all post-allocation exits; neither credentials nor creator cdhash are serialized to public diagnostics/Python.",
    "Real persisted access is read after ADD; all non-partition summary fields stay equal. Then a separate existing importer process freshly verifies its current code against the stored creator entry, requires exact four counts, and actually signs/verifies a fresh private-key challenge.",
    "Original real codesign commands, complete CMS/MachO/profile/explicit-anchor/ZIP verification, deletion and producer deadlines remain required. Any nonzero mutation/read/challenge/codesign status stays a nonzero failure.",
    "Public schema1 and schema2 remain byte-identical. Schema3 adds only bounded creatorPartitionCount, partitionACLAdded and creatorPartitionVerified facts; raw ACL/subject/cdhash/path/label/key/password output is still forbidden."
  ],
